From dbfc197791f6a5a50c816542b74a1d9cf8723e08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:57:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jank-18: small vectors, one GC allocation for vectors of up
 to 32 elements

Draft: cohost.cljc doc/upstream/jank-18-small-vectors.md
Files: compiler+runtime/include/cpp/jank/runtime/obj/persistent_vector.hpp,
       compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/runtime/obj/persistent_vector.cpp,
       compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/runtime/obj/transient_vector.cpp,
       compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/codegen/api.cpp
Repro: bash dev/research/upstream/run.sh 18-small-vectors (Expected: [i i] 2e6 within 3x of
       GC_MALLOC(16) 2e6; binary-trees depth 14 within 3x of the JVM's 8.7 ms)

persistent_vector::create_small lays out one GC_malloc block as
[persistent_vector | exact-size immer leaf] and makes the leaf the vector's tail
(root = immer's shared empty root). The result is an ordinary immer vector, so
nth, conj, assoc, pop, seq, equality, hash, transients, meta and printing are
the same code as before; growth past 32 moves the leaf into the tree as usual.
The general path built a stack transient: a 1-byte owner token, a full 32-slot
leaf (272 bytes) and then the box, three allocations.

- _jank_vec (vector literals and clojure.core/vector, which is defined by
  literals) of <= 32 elements without string meta: create_small.
- persistent_vector::conj below 32 elements: one block holding the old
  elements plus the new one (was: immer's leaf copy plus a separate box).
- _jank_vec collects its varargs in raw storage (a default object_ref loads
  jank_nil, 32 of them per literal) and the box is constructed in place over
  the rbtree (one immer move fewer).
- persistent_vector::find and transient_vector::find entries: create_small
  (was: the initializer_list path, i.e. owner token + full leaf + box).
- persistent_vector's meta moves out of line: a `lazy_meta *` allocated only
  for a vector that carries meta (an inline lazy_meta is a folly::Synchronized,
  a string and an ns: 48 of the box's 104 bytes). Each vector owns its own
  lazy_meta (conj/assoc/pop/copy copy it, as the by-value member did), read and
  published with std::atomic_ref; get_meta on a vector without meta no longer
  takes a lock. The box is 56 bytes, a two-element vector one 80-byte block.

The block is a plain conservatively scanned GC_malloc, never a typed
descriptor, so the elements in the trailing leaf are traced; jank runs bdwgc
with GC_set_all_interior_pointers(1), so the tail pointer alone keeps the block
alive when the immer value outlives its box. immer never frees or mutates the
leaf: the memory policy does no refcounting and the leaf has no transient
owner, so a transient or a persistent update copies it.
